Money from the Spalding County Emergency Telephone System Fund shall be used only to pay for:
(a) The lease, purchase, or maintenance of emergency telephone equipment, including necessary computer hardware, software, and data base provisioning; address; and nonrecurring costs of establishing the "911" system;
(b) The rates associated with the service supplier's "911" service and other service supplier's recurring charges;
(c) The actual cost of salaries of employees hired by the county solely for the operation and maintenance of the emergency "911" system;
(d) Office suppliers of the public safety answering points used directly in providing emergency "911" system services; and
(e) The cost of leasing or purchasing a building used as a public safety answering point.
The county may contract with a service supplier for any term negotiated by the service supplier and the county or an emergency "911" system and may make payments from the emergency telephone system fund to provide any payments required by the contract.
In order to provide additional funding for the county for emergency "911" system purposes, the county may receive federal, state, municipal, or private funds for the emergency telephone system fund which shall be expended for the purposes of this article. (Ord. No. 90-14, § 1, 9-4-90)

